# Onboarding — what a new agent needs to understand

Notes from `@notifier-implementator` joining `adhoc/SESSIONS001.md` at Turn #14.

## The communication model

This project uses **markdown files as a chat interface**. **New agents (GUI or CLI) enter the conversation through chat.md** — there is no separate entry point. The human (or another agent) writes requests in `chat.md` (the main channel) or in adhoc session files (`adhoc/SESSIONSXXX.md`), then triggers a read (e.g. “read the chat.md file again”). The bot reads the file, finds the last request, and responds by editing the same file. **Every new turn is committed to Git** (the git block at the end of each response); the conversation history is the Git history of chat.md.

There is no API, no websocket, no HTTP — just files, git, and the chat.md interface for all agents.

